# Demo Patch 4 — Trivy: HIGH/CRITICAL Filesystem CVE

## What it demonstrates
Trivy scans the repository filesystem and detects a package version with
a known HIGH or CRITICAL CVE. The gate blocks the deploy stage.

## Trigger
Downgrade a dependency to a version with known CVEs, or add a package
with a published HIGH/CRITICAL vulnerability.

Example: use `requests==2.19.0` (has multiple HIGH CVEs).

--- a/app/requirements.txt
+++ b/app/requirements.txt
@@ -1,2 +1,3 @@
 Flask==3.1.3
 gunicorn==22.0.0
+requests==2.19.0

## Expected gate output
app/requirements.txt (pip)
===========================
Total: 2 (HIGH: 1, CRITICAL: 1)

┌──────────┬────────────────┬──────────┬───────────────┬───────────────┐
│ Library  │ Vulnerability  │ Severity │ Installed Ver │ Fixed Version │
├──────────┼────────────────┼──────────┼───────────────┼───────────────┤
│ requests │ CVE-2023-XXXXX │ HIGH     │ 2.19.0        │ 2.31.0        │
│ urllib3  │ CVE-2023-YYYYY │ CRITICAL │ 1.23          │ 1.26.18       │
└──────────┴────────────────┴──────────┴───────────────┴───────────────┘

Error: Process completed with exit code 1.

## Fix
Upgrade requests to the fixed version. Verify no breaking changes.